P5,P5-two-windows-and-stacked-alerts-gtk4.actions,misaimed,"The main window shows Ready. and p5-debug-events.log lists C, B, A dismissed (stacking order now correct), but every line is Secondary:. After the second window opened, the clicks resolved against it, so the log has no Main: lines and the expected mix of windows is missing.","reworked (2fcb412a): Alert A on the secondary window, focus back to main for A+B+C; Secondary: A then Main: C B A"
P7,P7-two-lists-and-a-split-view.actions,ok,"End state matches: Selection: Cherry with plain-list Cherry highlighted, split list cleared (No sidebar selection), longer message added and the detail pane keeps its share; the earlier split-list clicks cannot be checked from the final frame.",
P8,P8-nested-scroll-views.actions,ok,"Outer view scrolled (Outer row 2 at the top), the red child sits inside the rounded corners and the H0-H9 strip is intact; the strip fits its width, so horizontal movement is not visible.",
P9,P9-field-height-and-clipped-text.actions,ok,"Field reads hi, the secure field shows 3 dots, updates: 2 with the field height unchanged against Reference, and zero width (0 px) shows no spill.",
P10,P10-overlays-and-hit-testing.actions,ok,"Direct clicks 2, Covered clicks 2, Hidden clicks 2, with the overlay toggle switched off, matching the stated end state.",
P10,P10-taplabel.actions,ok,"Direct 1, Covered 1, Hidden 1 and Hidden button received a click, as the three taplabel rows require.",
P11,P11-sliders-scrollbar-and-picker-gtk4.actions,ok,"minimum 50 / maximum 50 with both knobs at 50, writes min 3 max 0 (only the min slider is dragged, so max 0 is expected), list back at Row 1, hour 09 at 08:12 capture time = launch+1, date unchanged.",
P12,P12-tabs-margins-and-toggles-gtk4.actions,ok,"Selected tab: Second counter: 2, forced-on Toggle is filled and forced-off is outlined (look different), Switch is on.",
P13,P13-duplicates-split-width-and-z-order-gtk4.actions,ok,"More duplicates (5), Narrower (280) with Detail pane visible, and the red square now on top after Reverse; the Top of the stack label is hidden under the 150 pt red square that overflows its 220x110 ZStack frame (also over the Reverse button), a layout overlap worth noting but the z-order reading is correct.",
P14,P14-width-history-and-theme-control.actions,ok,"Count a rotation (3), Width history empty after Clear (Count does not append), and the status reads the #254 control's message so the control responded.",
P15,P15-colour-scheme-and-tall-content-gtk4.actions,ok,"Requested: dark Resolved: dark, field reads Editable textxy, six Extra rows shown and status reads Content is taller.",
P15-DARK,P15-DARK-button-under-an-overridden-scheme-gtk4.actions,ok,A button (1) with Requested: dark Resolved: dark.,
P16,P16-split-view-columns-gtk4.actions,ok,"Force update (3), three columns shown (button reads Switch to 2 column), sidebar Humanities selected, middle Humanities, Detail for Humanities.",
P17,P17-picker-aspect-ratio-and-stack-height-gtk4.actions,ok,"presses: SML--++<> and stack: 145 x 140 with Less height (140), as required.",
P17-DOE,P17-DOE-the-control-clips-too.actions,ok,"No-op file whose header describes AppKit (all three clipped); on GTK the control spills 80 pt above and below while A and B are clipped to 120 pt, which is the intended DOE contrast and SwiftUI-correct, so the AppKit claim does not apply rather than GTK being wrong.",
P18,P18-open-and-cancel-each-dialog-gtk4.actions,ok,"open -> cancelled, folder -> cancelled, save -> cancelled.",
P19,P19-open-the-menu-gtk4.actions,misaimed,"toggle item -> true is correct but last action reads second button item instead of button item: after Escape and reopen, one Down landed on the second button item (GTK apparently restores focus to the previously activated toggle row), so the key count is off by one for the reopened menu.",items now clicked (2fcb412a): the keyboard start position in a GTK popover menu varies between runs; queue item 22
P20,P20-open-the-nested-menu-gtk4.actions,ok,last action -> level 3 and level 3 toggle -> true.,
P21,P21-enabled-and-disabled-gtk4.actions,ok,"Button clicks 1, Toggle true, ToggleSwitch false, Toggle button style true, Checkbox true; disabled twins unchanged.",
P21,P21-lower-half-gtk4.actions,defect,"The 120-notch wheel scrolled the content only about 80 pt (title gone, Button row still near the top), so the derived clicks hit empty space and nothing changed (clicks 0, all toggles at launch state, no fields visible); same ~80 pt-per-scroll-event pattern as P22 and P11 suggests the wheel delta magnitude is dropped (one fixed step per event) rather than an aim error.","fixed 244ed158: one wheel event per notch, posted off the main thread; re-run reaches the lower half and types into the fields"
P22,P22-wrapping-width-and-scroll.actions,defect,"Wrapping at 350pt is correct, but after +6, +6, -12 notches the view is not back at the top (title and backend lines scrolled off by about 80 pt), consistent with each scroll event moving one fixed step regardless of notch count.","fixed 244ed158: vadjustment read 78.8 157.7 78.8 before, 307 then 0 after; re-run back at the top, Wrapping at 350pt"
P23,P23-click-a-row-gtk4.actions,defect,"Reads selected row: 2 with row 3 highlighted; the click at frame (100,581) is inside row 5 (frame y ~568-596) yet the selection did not move to row 4, so GTK Table click-to-select is not working, as the file's own criterion states.","fixed fdb29e74: Gtk.Table finds the cell from the cells' bounds when the pick cannot; SELECTION now 4, row 5 highlighted"
P23,P23-column-sorting-gtk4.actions,ok,"sort: column 3 descending, Number header shows a down arrow, first/last id 8/1 and rows run 8,7,6,5,4.",
P23,P23-row-selection-gtk4.actions,ok,selected row: 2 with row 3 highlighted as required; the claimed log line SELECTION now 4 from the row click cannot be checked (p23-debug-events.log was overwritten by a later run) and P23-click-a-row suggests that row click does not select.,
P23,P23-rows-and-selection.actions,misaimed,"rows: 16 (8 +4x4 -2x4) and Selection on are correct, but the drag at frame y 267 (AppKit row-1 coordinate) landed on the selected row label line, not on row 1 (frame y ~470), so the drag-across-a-cell check was not exercised.","new P23-rows-and-selection-gtk4.actions (2fcb412a): drag at y 470 across row 1's third cell; rows 16, Selection on, text selected"
