P34,P34-more-rows-and-scrolling-gtk4.actions,ok,"Header reads requested rows: 500; showing first 500 and the list top is Row 5, so the wheel reached the list (20 notches moved only about 5 rows, which is past Row 0 but modest).",
P35,P35-state-baseline.actions,ok,"State baseline: count 4, toggle false, exactly as required.",
P36,P36-picker-button-and-textfield-gtk4.actions,ok,Text field reads SwiftCrossUI TextField12 with the caret at the end and the pickers closed on Vanilla.,
P37,P37-floating-level-and-what-a-replay-cannot-do.actions,ok,"Reads supported levels -> automatic, normal, floating and floating is supported: this window should stay in front; backend line says GtkBackend (the file's AppKitBackend line is backend-specific).",
P38,P38-scroll-the-web-view.actions,defect,Option-Tab reached the page (Learn more has a focus ring) but Return did not follow it: Navigations reported: 1 and the frame still shows example.com instead of 2 and the IANA page (network failure not fully ruled out).,"fixed d68b40ac: keys reach a focused WKWebView through a capture controller on the GTK window; Navigations reported 2, IANA page scrolled"
P39,P39-read-nine-cells-against-the-control.actions,unclear,"All nine cells differ from the control, but saturation 0 and grayscale 1 are pixel-identical at every probe (138/134/136/103/159/191 in both) where the file says they must be different greys; GtkBackend emits CSS saturate(0) and grayscale(1), which the CSS filter spec defines identically, so this is not miswiring but does not meet the file's claim.",noted: CSS saturate(0) and grayscale(1) are one operation by spec; the AppKit 94 is CIColorMonochrome tinted with grey 0.5 -- which is right is open
P40,P40-read-seven-tiles-and-the-clipping.actions,ok,"All seven tiles transformed and spilling outside their slots with no neighbour moved (unlike the clipped AppKit result the file records), and centre vs topLeading rotations differ.",
P41,P41-three-date-picker-styles-gtk4.actions,misaimed,"Dates read .automatic 2025-08-24, .compact 2025-08-24, .graphical 2025-08-03 instead of 09-24/09-24/08-17: the layout sits about 37pt lower than measured, so the popover-opening clicks (y 263, 431) hit above the buttons (now at y 300, 469) and the graphical click at y 303 hit day 3 instead of 17 (now at y 340).",re-aimed +37 pt (2fcb412a): the content is shorter now that .hourMinuteAndSecond does not wrap per character; 09-24 09-24 08-17
